#: src/redoxfs.md:1
msgid "RedoxFS"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:3
msgid ""
"This is the default filesystem of Redox OS, inspired by ZFS and adapted to a "
"microkernel architecture."
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:5
msgid ""
"Redox had a read-only ZFS driver but it was abandoned because of the "
"monolithic nature of ZFS that created problems with the Redox microkernel "
"design."
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:7
msgid ""
"(It's a replacement for [TFS](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/tfs))"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:9
msgid "Current features:"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:11
msgid "Compatible with Redox and Linux (FUSE)"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:12
msgid "Copy-on-write"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:13
msgid "Data/metadata checksums"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:14
msgid "Transparent encryption"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:15
msgid "Standard Unix file attributes"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:16
msgid "File/directory size limit up to 193TiB (212TB)"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:17
msgid ""
"File/directory quantity limit up to 4 billion per 193TiB (2^32 - 1 = "
"4294967295)"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:18
msgid ""
"Disk encryption fully supported by the Redox bootloader, letting it load the "
"kernel off an encrypted partition."
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:19
msgid "MIT licensed"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:21
msgid ""
"Being MIT licensed, RedoxFS can be bundled on GPL-licensed operating systems "
"(Linux, for example)."
msgstr ""

