#: src/redoxfs.md:171
msgid "Working with Linux Partition"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:173
msgid ""
"⚠️ **Warning:** Experimental and dangerous; always double-check your command "
"before executing it."
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:175
msgid ""
"On Linux, RedoxFS supports formatting and mounting directly from `/dev` "
"partition. [Redox OS GUI installer](./installing.md) also supports "
"formatting and installing into a whole disk or specific partition. This "
"guide only covers the manual process using `redoxfs` CLI tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:177
msgid "Creating an empty partition for RedoxFS"
msgstr ""

#: src/redoxfs.md:179
msgid ""
"First thing you need to do is that you need to create an empty space for "
"RedoxFS partition to fit in. Use [GParted](https://gparted.org/), [GNOME "
"Disks](https://apps.gnome.org/DiskUtility/) or [KDE Partition Manager]"
"(https://apps.kde.org/partitionmanager/) to create an empty partition, then "
"identify the partition using `lsblk`"
msgstr ""

